@startuml
title Target Architecture - Extensible Entity Models

!pragma layout smetana
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "Simulation Runtime" {
  [SimulationRunner] as Runner
  [Canonical EntityState] as State
  interface IEntityModel
  interface ISensorModel
  interface IBehaviorModel
  interface IController
  interface ICommunicationAdapter
  [Model Manifest and Registry] as Registry
}

package "In-process models" {
  [Kinematic model] as Kinematic
  [JSBSim model] as JSBSim
  [Native C ABI plugin] as Native
  [FMI 2.0 / FMI 3.0 adapter] as FMI
}

package "External models and federations" {
  [HLA / DIS / DDS] as SimProtocols
  [ROS 2 / gRPC / ZeroMQ] as ProcessProtocols
  [C2SIM / MSDL adapters] as C2
  [Optional MIXR providers] as MIXR
}

package "World Services" {
  interface IGeospatialService
  interface ITerrainElevationService
  interface IWeatherService
  interface ICollisionService
}

Runner --> IEntityModel : configure / initialize / step / reset / shutdown
Runner --> ISensorModel
Runner --> IBehaviorModel
Runner --> IController
Runner --> ICommunicationAdapter
Runner --> State
Registry --> Runner

IEntityModel <|.. Kinematic
IEntityModel <|.. JSBSim
IEntityModel <|.. Native
IEntityModel <|.. FMI
ICommunicationAdapter <|.. SimProtocols
ICommunicationAdapter <|.. ProcessProtocols
ICommunicationAdapter <|.. C2
ISensorModel <|.. MIXR

Runner --> IGeospatialService
Runner --> ITerrainElevationService
Runner --> IWeatherService
Runner --> ICollisionService

note right of Registry
Declares units, frames, vertical datum,
timestep, determinism, version, license,
capabilities and save/restore support.
end note

note bottom of State
Technology-neutral state shared by
runtime, UI, persistence and adapters.
end note

@enduml
